  {
    "@id": "https://www.lediamant.ca/temporary/3c7c732a-12e1-4a57-9fec-0e50b3ebc2c2",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Play"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.lediamant.ca/en/programming/humans"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.lediamant.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Visuel-Humans-700x700.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.lediamant.ca/en/programming/humans"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Humans"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Ten acrobats take us on an emotional journey, where we discover what it means to be human through the way our bodies, relationships, and aspirations shape who we are. By pushing the physical limits of their bodies to the extreme, they question the weight we can carry as humans. And also: who can we lean on? They prompt us to reflect on our lives, our loved ones, the burdens we carry, and the physical and emotional strength required to overcome them.\nCreated by Yaron Lifschitz, the stage is stripped bare, mirroring the vulnerability of a highly skilled team of acrobats. With strength and integrity, they connect each moment to the next, weaving a thrilling and astonishing performance. Witness their humanity as they discover redemptive power and fiercely celebrate what it means to be human.\nCIRCA may well be the most sought-after Australian artistic company in the world right now, with a touring schedule that&#8217;s dizzying. The essence of Circa as daring and ambitious new circus is its reputation, found in every one of its shows, which combine physical virtuosity with expressive humanism.\n"
      }
    ]
  },
